sis and Design\n- CONTAINS: Statistics for Computing\n- CONTAINS: Social Issues and Professional Practice\n- CONTAINS: Wireless Technologies and Network Programming\n- CONTAINS: Data communications and networks\n- CONTAINS: Human-Computer Interaction\n- CONTAINS: Advanced Mathematics for Computing\n- CONTAINS: Computer Architecture\n- CONTAINS: Cryptography\n- CONTAINS: Operating Systems\n- CONTAINS: Platform-Based Development\n- CONTAINS: Data Warehousing and Data Mining\n- CONTAINS: Business Policy and Strategy\n- CONTAINS: Object-Oriented Programming with Java\n- CONTAINS: Enterprise Networks\n- CONTAINS: Algorithms and Data structures\n- CONTAINS: E-Business Application Development\n- CONTAINS: IT Project Management\n- CONTAINS: Management Information Systems\n- CONTAINS: Web-Based Application Development\n- CONTAINS: Embedded Systems\n- CONTAINS: IT Audit and Control\n- CONTAINS: Enterprise Architecture\n- CONTAINS: Entrepreneurship\n- CONTAINS: Disaster Recovery and High availability Techniques\n- CONTAINS: CN Honours Award Project\n- CONTAINS: Network Management\n- CONTAINS: Voice and Video over IP\n- CONTAINS: Network systems configuration and administration\n- CONTAINS: Network Security\n- CONTAINS: Advanced Routing and Switching\n- CONTAINS: Service provider systems and networks\n- CONTAINS: Intrusion Prevention, Detection & Response\n\nThought:  This course, "Computer Networks," falls under the broader discipline of Computer Science. It focuses on teaching students how to design, implement, and manage computer networks in a data science context. Key topics include network protocols, architecture, security, and troubleshooting common issues that can arise on computer networks.\n\nThis course is closely related to other subjects within Computer Science such as Mathematics for Computing, Programming in C, Database Management Systems, Professional Development, and Development of Enterprise Applications I. It also covers Information Assurance and Security, Internship opportunities, and Systems Analysis and Design.\n\nAdditional topics include Wireless Technologies and Network Programming, Data communications and networks, Human-Computer Interaction, Advanced Mathematics for Computing, Computer Architecture, Cryptography, Operating Systems, Platform-Based Development, Data Warehousing and Data Mining, Business Policy and Strategy, Object-Oriented Programming with Java, Enterprise Networks, Algorithms and Data structures, E-Business Application Development, IT Project Management, Management Information Systems, Web-Based Application Development, Embedded Systems, IT Audit and Control, Entrepreneurship, Disaster Recovery and High availability Techniques, and more.\n\nThe course also covers specific areas like Network Management, Voice and Video over IP, Network systems configuration and administration, Network Security, Advanced Routing and Switching, Service provider systems and networks, Intrusion Prevention, Detection & Response, and Network Management.\nObservation: Invalid Format: Missing \'Action:\' after \'Thought:\nThought: ']
