2024-11-26 13:45:00,902 - __main__ - DEBUG - LLM Start - Prompts: ['Answer the following questions as best you can. You have access to the following tools:\n\ngraph_query(query: str) -> str - Query the academic knowledge graph for courses, prerequisites, and relationships\nsemantic_search(query: str) -> str - Search for semantically similar content using vector embeddings\n\nUse the following format:\n\nQuestion: the input question you must answer\nThought: you should always think about what to do\nAction: the action to take, should be one of [graph_query, semantic_search]\nAction Input: the input to the action\nObservation: the result of the action\n... (this Thought/Action/Action Input/Observation can repeat N times)\nThought: I now know the final answer\nFinal Answer: the final answer to the original input question\n\nBegin!\n\nQuestion: hello. I want to know about data science\nThought: To answer this question, I need to gather information about data science. Since the question is broad and there might be various aspects to cover, it would be best to use both graph_query and semantic_search.\n\nAction: graph_query\nAction Input: "data science"\nObservation: 📚 Data Science\nDescription: \nThe Data Science course is designed to provide students with a comprehensive understanding of the field of data science, including its applications, methodologies, and tools. The course will cover topics such as data preprocessing, statistical modeling, machine learning, and visualization, all with an emphasis on practical application in real-world scenarios. Students will learn how to collect, manipulate, and analyze large datasets, and how to make informed decisions based on the insights gained from data analysis. The course will also cover topics such as data ethics, privacy, and security, and how to work with diverse data types, including text, images, and structured data.\nRelated items:\n- CONTAINS: Introduction to Computer Science\n- CONTAINS: Introduction to Data Science\n- CONTAINS: Web Mining\n- CONTAINS: Natural Language Processing\n- CONTAINS: Mathematics for Computing\n- CONTAINS: Human Computer Interaction\n- CONTAINS: Advanced Statistics for Data Science\n- CONTAINS: Neural Networks\n- CONTAINS: Programming in C\n- CONTAINS: Data Programming with R\n- CONTAINS: Data Warehousing & Data Mining\n- CONTAINS: Big Data Programming\n- CONTAINS: Database Management Systems\n- CONTAINS: Statistics for Data Science\n- CONTAINS: Data Visualization\n- CONTAINS: DS Honors Award Project\n- CONTAINS: Professional Development\n- CONTAINS: Introduction to Software Engineering\n- CONTAINS: Advanced database Management Systems\n- CONTAINS: Urban Computing\n- CONTAINS: Object Oriented Programming with Java\n- CONTAINS: Development of Enterprise Applications I\n- CONTAINS: Information Assurance and Security\n- CONTAINS: Artificial Intelligence\n- CONTAINS: Algorithms and Data Structures\n- CONTAINS: System Fundamentals\n- CONTAINS: Internship\n- CONTAINS: Data Science Trends and Applications\n- CONTAINS: Fundamentals of Computer Architecture\n- CONTAINS: Algorithms and Complexity\n- CONTAINS: Cloud Computing\n- CONTAINS: Deep Learning\n- CONTAINS: Data Communication and Networks\n- CONTAINS: Data Science in Python\n- CONTAINS: Machine Learning\n- CONTAINS: Parallel and Distributed Computing\n- CONTAINS: Web Based Application Development\n- CONTAINS: Ethics in Data Science\n- CONTAINS: Mobile Application Development\n- CONTAINS: Internet of Things\n- CONTAINS: Big Data Analytics\n- CONTAINS: Development of Enterprise Applications II\n\n📚 Computer Science\nDescription: \n"Explore the fundamental concepts and principles of computer science, including algorithms, data structures, programming languages, and software development methods. Learn how to apply these concepts to real-world problems in data science, enabling you to analyze and manipulate large datasets and build intelligent systems that make informed decisions."\nRelated items:\n- CONTAINS: Introduction to Computer Science\n- CONTAINS: Mathematics for Computing\n- CONTAINS: Programming in C\n- CONTAINS: Database Management Systems\n- CONTAINS: Professional Development\n- CONTAINS: Introduction to Software Engineering\n- CONTAINS: Object Oriented Programming with Java\n- CONTAINS: Development of Enterprise Applications I\n- CONTAINS: Information Assurance and Security\n- CONTAINS: Algorithms and Data Structures\n- CONTAINS: Internship\n- CONTAINS: Algorithms and Complexity\n- CONTAINS: Web Based Application Development\n- CONTAINS: Mobile Application Development\n- CONTAINS: Computer Networks\n- CONTAINS: Systems Analysis and Design\n- CONTAINS: Statistics for Computing\n- CONTAINS: Social Issues and Professional Practice\n- CONTAINS: Wireless Technologies and Network Programming\n- CONTAINS: Data communications and networks\n- CONTAINS: Human-Computer Interaction\n- CONTAINS: Advanced Mathematics for Computing\n- CONTAINS: Business Processes and ERP\n- CONTAINS: Computational Theory\n- CONTAINS:   Programming Languages and Compiler Design\n- CONTAINS: Computer Architecture\n- CONTAINS: Software Architecture\n- CONTAINS: Advanced Database Management Systems\n- CONTAINS: Cryptography\n- CONTAINS: Operating Systems\n- CONTAINS: Software Process Management\n\n📚 Software Engineering\nDescription: \nCourse Title: Software Engineering for Data Science\n\nCourse Description: This course will provide an introduction to software engineering concepts and practices that are particularly relevant to data science projects. Students will learn about software development methodologies, testing, debugging, version control, and collaboration tools used in data science projects. The course will also cover the ethical considerations of data science, including issues related to bias, privacy, and transparency.\n\nCourse Outline:\n\n1. Introduction to Software Engineering for Data Science\n2. Project Planning and Management\n3. Testing and Debugging Techniques in Data Science\n4. Version Control Systems and Collaboration Tools\n5. Ethical Considerations in Data Science\n6. Advanced Topics in Data Science Software Engineering\n7. Final Project Presentation and Evaluation\n\nCourse Learning Outcomes:\n\n* Understand the fundamental concepts of software engineering for data science projects\n* Be able to plan, manage, and execute a data science project with software engineering principles in mind\n* Apply testing and debugging techniques to identify and fix issues in data science code\n* Use version control systems and collaboration tools effectively in data science projects\n* Understand the ethical considerations of data science and how they impact software development\n* Be able to apply advanced software engineering concepts to real-world data science projects\n\nCourse Level: Graduate\n\nCourse Format: Online, self-paced course with weekly video lectures and interactive activities.\nRelated items:\n- CONTAINS: Introduction to Computer Science\n- CONTAINS: Mathematics for Computing\n- CONTAINS: Programming in C\n- CONTAINS: Database Management Systems\n- CONTAINS: Professional Development\n- CONTAINS: Development of Enterprise Applications I\n- CONTAINS: Information Assurance and Security\n- CONTAINS: Artificial Intelligence\n- CONTAINS: Internship\n- CONTAINS: Algorithms and Complexity\n- CONTAINS: Parallel and Distributed Computing\n- CONTAINS: Mobile Application Development\n- CONTAINS: Internet of Things\n- CONTAINS: Development of Enterprise Applications II\n- CONTAINS: Computer Networks\n- CONTAINS: Systems Analysis and Design\n- CONTAINS: Statistics for Computing\n- CONTAINS: Social Issues and Professional Practice\n- CONTAINS: Data communications and networks\n- CONTAINS: Human-Computer Interaction\n- CONTAINS: Advanced Mathematics for Computing\n- CONTAINS: Business Processes and ERP\n- CONTAINS: Computer Architecture\n- CONTAINS: Software Architecture\n- CONTAINS: Advanced Database Management Systems\n- CONTAINS: Operating